**Read:** [Sabão e detergentes — Heizir F. de Castro](../sources/Saboes-e-Detergentes-Castro.lingua#r_08ET1T9T2F8GDEB1315ZB6XFRF), the entire soap/detergent chemistry, production and formulation apostila; [Organic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../sources/Organic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_1ERYESBGNKCKMDY0NPHJKCVJG0), the complete soaps/detergents manufacturing sequence; [Óleos e gorduras — Heizir F. de Castro](../sources/Oleos-e-Gorduras-Castro.lingua#r_4C89Z0YDFDBY55HN2R7WCDEETY), the full feed-composition, refining and modification context.

Soap production links feed lipids or fatty acids with the chemical form of a surfactant, while synthetic detergent routes create other surfactant structures and mixtures. Surfactant identity, chain distribution, counterions, water conditions, concentration and other ingredients influence interfacial and cleaning behavior.

An ideal saponification or neutralization relation provides a stoichiometric account but not a complete product process. Feed composition, conversion, co-products such as glycerol, separation, salt/water, drying and formulation change the delivered material. Distinguish active surfactant amount from total product mass.

Performance and environmental fate need the actual application and evidence. A favorable foam observation does not establish cleaning, stability or downstream behavior. Formulation, packaging/contact materials and storage can alter the physical/chemical state before use.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public soap or detergent route and its actual functional tests. Independently close feed/reagent, surfactant, co-product, water and residual accounts. Compare a documented feed/route/formulation alternative on equal useful function, explain the phase/interfacial and analytical basis of the comparison and identify a changed-condition test capable of challenging it.

**Continue:** [Follow carbohydrate feeds through preparation, separation and further chemical use](Sugar-starch-concentration-crystallization-and-platform-feeds.lingua#r_0GFTR01N55B1VRJV8JZMA30KZJ).

**Return:** [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618).
